The baseline for the closure/suspension representation work
(/work/plans/closure-conformance-plan.md). Seven of its ten programs pass
every cell; the three Rust programs do not compile, because the Rust member
spells one morloc function type five different ways and the conversions
between them do not compose. That is the D3 redesign target
(/work/plans/d3-rust-closure-representation.md).

Runnable now: `make` builds and runs the ten programs, `make cells` builds
each (program, cell) alone so one red does not mask the rest. Remove this
file when D3 lands and every cell is green in all ten programs; that is the
acceptance test for the redesign. Doing so also needs an exp.txt holding the
output of a green run -- the directory has none, which is why the SKIP is
checked before the Makefile and exp.txt are.
